From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:45:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Optimise: free worlds left behind, fewer lights, density
 1.25, come back after a lost GPU

- Only the world you are in and the next stay mounted; a world left behind frees its geometries,
  materials and textures (city 159 -> 112 MB of textures, cave 166 -> 80 MB, programs halved).
- Lights: the station's masts behind the door and the street's far pair of lamps only glow; the
  moving cars' headlights are their drawn beam, not lights (station 13 -> 8 spots, city 14 -> 9);
  two shadow casters per world.
- Pixel density at most 1.25.
- When the browser takes WebGL away and does not give it back, the page reloads and comes back to
  the chapter you were in, with your sound setting, without asking again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
